= Use Case  [UC02] =

//Declared and deliberately deferred, so the scope decision is explicit rather than implicit in what happened to get written first.//

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC02
|Name|Support the resident through the medication routine
|Status|Not Started
|Evidence basis|Would formalize SA-02 and PS-02. No primary data collected by this project.
|Scope decision|(((
SA-02 and SA-01 have different triggers and different Goals, so this is a separate Use Case rather than an alternate flow of UC01 - it is not a candidate for merging.

It is deferred for this cycle rather than dropped. Reasons:

- PS-02's out-of-scope field already narrows it heavily, including a care-home blacklist for residents on critical medication, which needs settling before Functions can be written.

- PS-02 adds a fourth sub-problem, confirmation, that has no counterpart in PS-01 - the resident failing to confirm they have taken the medication, risking a double dose. That needs its own Function and its own Claim, and possibly a safety Premise, rather than reusing F1-F4.

- Specifying it properly would roughly double the Premise and Claim count, and the medication activity will need Measures of its own on the §1.2 Measures page, numbered from M-09.

F1-F4 are expected to transfer, since both activities are stepwise sequences with initiation, sequencing and completion breakdowns. Confirming that recurrence across two Use Cases is what would justify abstracting the TDP and IDP in Steps 12-13 - so UC02 should be written before those are finalized, not after.

Group decision (Open item O-13): tooth brushing is this cycle's spine. Material already written for medication is kept for UC02 rather than discarded: DS-02 (§2.1), the tray or dispenser option TECH-06 (§1.3), and the medication-timing tension VT-06 (§1.2).
)))

