|O-1|Resolved. M-01…M-07 are on the §1.2 [[4. Measures>>Main.b\. Human Factors.3\. Measures.WebHome]] page and EM-01…EM-03 on the §1.2 [[5. Evaluation Methods>>Main.b\. Human Factors.Measuring Instruments.WebHome]] page. New Measures start at M-09 (M-08 Brushing quality was added for O-23), new Evaluation Methods at EM-04.|Nothing|Closed
|O-2|Resolved (group decision: in scope). Notifying a care worker on immediate risk of serious harm stays in F3 and step 10. VT-01's non-negotiable floor now says "none identified", and the escalation rule has moved into its current resolution, since it is a design decision, not a regulation. PS-02's out-of-scope now excludes only emergency //treatment//. Because there is no camera, a possible emergency is inferred from no sensor change and no response (TECH-02 limitation, step 10).|Nothing|Closed
